damian@ubuntu:~$ # in this lab i will reproduce the error i found by
# chance in october 2026. while learning ufw and
# firewalld i tried to prove firewalld is not installed
# on ubuntu. it was in fact installed and running,
# probably from an older session when a rocky system
# was unavailable to me, so an older install of
# firewalld was still present on ubuntu. therefore any
# packet this system received had to comply with both
# firewalld and ufw rules, and firewalld running on an
# ubuntu system would easily pass unnoticed when
# troubleshooting a drop/deny packet issue
